KNOWNBUG
JmlForall
--function JmlForall.identity --jml-source src/main/java/JmlForall.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
KNOWNBUG: \forall in JML preconditions / postconditions.

The JML parser correctly produces forall_exprt nodes, but JBMC's
symex pipeline doesn't currently know how to bind the
quantifier's bound variable. The error manifests as:

    Invariant check failed
    Condition: found_l0
    Reason: level0: failed to find i

To unblock this test, JBMC needs one of:
  (a) Skolemization of universally-quantified preconditions
      (replace forall var. P(var) with assume P(nondet_var())).
  (b) Bounded expansion analogous to the \sum/\product handling
      in jml_lowering.cpp, when the range bounds are constant.
  (c) A symex-level lowering of forall/exists to native CBMC
      quantifier instructions.

Until one of those lands, this test stays KNOWNBUG so the
intent is captured but the suite stays green.
